// Kona (コナビ) Language Examples
// Purely functional, acoustically engineered syntax for AI agents
//
// Every line below compiles. Verify with:
//   python3 kona.py "$(sed -n '8p' example.kona)"

// 1. Deep code analysis, guarded dry-run edit, tabular output
kwe.de @repo:"security" |> tori.ve @code !"migrations" |> fasa #table

// 2. Web query and structured JSON extraction
//    Arguments use @target:"value" -- parentheses open a nested pipeline.
kwe @web:"AWS Azure Q3 revenue" |> fasa #json

// 3. Conditional deployment with fallback
si teli bono |> yuki @task :else: fasa @bug

// 4. Multi-target device inspection
visi @cam @display |> teli |> do @msg

// 5. Spoken form of example 1 -- compiles to the identical AST
dekwe poya "security" te, vetori kodo notori "migrations" te, fasa mesa

// 6. Nested pipeline, numerals (nipaduwo = 120) and scoping
si teli bono te, (kwe nipaduwo ina poya te, fasa poti) ali fasa baki

// 7. Grammatical aspect: progressive, perfective, habitual
yukiba te, makita te, fasasa
